  "gaps": [
    "The capture spans several programs (Communication Studies fragment, Computer Information Systems, and a truncated Computer Science section); this ledger assumes the intended program is the BS in Computer Information Systems, the only one with complete requirements in the capture.",
    "The capture says only 'credits' and never names the credit unit (semester vs. quarter); 'semester' was selected because the schema requires a value, but the unit is not stated in the capture.",
    "Residency rules are not tied to specific courses: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) must be completed at UMGC, half the credits within the major must be completed at UMGC, and at least 15 upper-level credits must be completed at UMGC. Which specific requirements satisfy these is not determinable from the capture, so no item is flagged institutionalOnly.",
    "Specific major elective course choices depend on the student; the capture lists eligible courses and recommended focus areas only.",
    "General education courses shown in the course-sequencing table (e.g., PACE 111T, LIBS 150, STAT 200, CMSC 105, WRTG 393) are recommendations, not fixed requirements, so gen-ed blocks are recorded by category.",
    "Credits for related/business core are not listed for this major; the CIS degree table shows none."
